.TH OED 1 "2026-10-02" "OED2 CLI 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oed \- Oxford English Dictionary 2nd Edition (OED2) reader, query engine, and interactive shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oed
[\fB\-f\fR \fIDAT_FILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B oed lookup
\fIword\fR
[\fB\-\-all\fR|\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-\-raw\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed end
\fIsuffix\fR
[\fB\-\-single\fR|\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-\-len\fR|\fB\-l\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed text
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-full\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed search
\fIprefix\fR
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed random
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed info
.br
.B oed block
\fInumber\fR
[\fB\-\-raw\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed export
\fIoutput_file\fR
.br
.B oed shell
[\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR]
.br
.B oed man

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oed
provides high-performance, random-access lookup and exploration of the
Oxford English Dictionary 2nd Edition (20 volumes, ~290,000 entries)
directly from a mounted CD-ROM ISO image or raw
.B OED2.DAT
data file.
.PP
The dictionary's proprietary Huffman and dictionary-symbol bitstream
compression is decoded on-the-fly without requiring disk extraction or
pre-installation. Entries are parsed from SGML into structured cards
featuring IPA phonetic transcriptions, etymologies, hierarchical
definitions (senses and sub-senses), and historical quotations.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIDAT_FILE\fR ", " \-\-dat\-file " " \fIDAT_FILE\fR
Specify the explicit path to the
.B OED2.DAT
file. If omitted,
.B oed
searches common mount points including
.IR /Volumes/OED2/OED2.DAT ,
.IR /Volumes/OED/OED2.DAT ,
the current working directory, and environment variables.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-pager
Disable interactive terminal paging. Output will stream continuously
without pausing. Paging is also automatically disabled when standard
output is not a terminal (e.g. when piped to another program).

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR lookup " " \fIword\fR " [" \-\-all | \-a "] [" \-\-raw "]"
Look up a headword in the dictionary using binary search across compressed blocks.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-all ", " \-a
Display all recorded historical quotations for the entry rather than just
the earliest citations.
.TP
.BR \-\-raw
Output unformatted, raw decompressed SGML markup directly.
.RE

.TP
.BR end " " \fIsuffix\fR " [" \-\-single | \-s "] [" \-\-len | \-l "] [" \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR | \-n " " \fIN\fR "]"
Search for dictionary headwords ending with the given letters or suffix
(e.g.,
.B oed end og
returns
.IR dog ,
.IR log ,
.IR bog ,
.IR clog ,
.IR frog ,
etc.).
Aliases:
.BR suffix ,
.BR ends\-with .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-single
Restrict results to single root words, excluding hyphenated terms and
multi-word phrases.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-len
Sort matched words by length first (shortest words first), then alphabetically.
.TP
.BR \-n " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR
Limit the number of displayed results to \fIN\fR words.
.RE

.TP
.BR text " " \fIquery\fR " [" \-\-full "] [" \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR | \-n " " \fIN\fR "] [" \-y | \-\-yes "]"
Search for a substring within the entire text of the dictionary (across all
7,829 compressed blocks). If more than 50 entries match, warns the user
and prompts for confirmation before displaying.
Aliases:
.BR fulltext ,
.BR find\-text .
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-full
Display complete formatted dictionary entries instead of snippet context cards.
.TP
.BR \-n " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR
Limit the number of displayed matching entries to \fIN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Automatically proceed without confirmation prompt if more than 50 entries match.
.RE

.TP
.BR search " " \fIprefix\fR
Search for headwords starting with the specified prefix (e.g.,
.BR "oed search electr" ).

.TP
.BR random
Retrieve and display a randomly selected entry from across the dictionary.

.TP
.BR info
Print metadata about the mounted CD-ROM volume, byte offsets, block sizes,
and decompressor status.

.TP
.BR block " " \fInumber\fR " [" \-\-raw "]"
Decompress and inspect a specific 32 KB block (valid range: 0 to 7828).
Displays decompressed size and headword catalog.

.TP
.BR export " " \fIoutput_file\fR
Decompress all 7,829 blocks sequentially and write the complete, contiguous
SGML text stream (~606 MB) to disk with real-time progress percentage.

.TP
.BR shell
Launch the interactive dictionary REPL. If no command is provided, the shell
launches automatically.

.TP
.BR man
Display this manual page.

.SH INTERACTIVE SHELL
When running
.B oed shell
(or running
.B oed
without arguments), an interactive prompt
.B OED>
is displayed.
.PP
.B Available Shell Commands:
.TP
.B <word>
Look up the specified word (e.g.,
.BR "OED> computer" ).
.TP
.B <word> \-\-all \fRor\fB <word> \-a \fRor\fB :all <word>
Look up the word and include all historical quotations.
.TP
.B <word> \-\-raw \fRor\fB :raw <word>
Look up the word and display raw decompressed SGML markup.
.TP
.B :text <query> [--full] [-n N] \fRor\fB text <query>
Search the entire text of the dictionary for a substring (e.g.
.BR "OED> :text pin"
or
.BR "OED> :text slide rule" ).
If more than 50 matching entries are found, prompts for confirmation before displaying.
.TP
.B :end <suffix> [-s] [-l] [-n N] \fRor\fB end <suffix>
Search words ending with the given suffix. For example:
.br
.B OED> :end og
.br
.B OED> :end og -s
(single root words only)
.br
.B OED> :end og --len
(sort by word length)
.TP
.B :search <prefix>
Search words by prefix (e.g.,
.BR "OED> :search astro" ).
.TP
.B :random
Display a random dictionary entry.
.TP
.B :block <number>
Inspect a specific block index (e.g.,
.BR "OED> :block 42" ).
.TP
.B :man
View this manual page.
.TP
.B :quit\fR, \fB:q\fR, \fB:exit
Exit the interactive shell. Note that typing common English words like
.I quit
or
.I exit
will search for their definitions in the dictionary; to exit, prepend
with a colon (
.BR :q
) or press
.B Ctrl\-D
/
.BR Ctrl\-C .

.SH BUILT-IN PAGER
Output exceeding the terminal screen height automatically pauses at the
end of each screen:
.TP
.B Space bar
Advance by one full screen (Page Down).
.TP
.B Enter / Return
Advance by one line.
.TP
.B q
Quit the pager immediately and return to the prompt or terminal.

.SH CACHING & PERFORMANCE
.TP
.B C Decompression Accelerator
On initial execution,
.B oed
compiles a tiny C shared library into
.I ~/.cache/oed/oed_decompress.so
using the system C compiler (
.B clang
or
.BR gcc ).
This accelerates block decompression to over 2,800 blocks per second.
If a C compiler is not present, a pure-Python fallback is used automatically.
.TP
.B Headword Index
When suffix search (
.BR :end
) is first invoked,
.B oed
catalogs all ~265,000 unique headwords across all 7,829 blocks into
.I ~/.cache/oed/headwords.tsv
(a one-time ~3 second process).
All subsequent prefix and suffix searches load in under 70 milliseconds and
search in under 15 milliseconds.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OED_DAT
Explicit filesystem path to the
.B OED2.DAT
file.
.TP
.B OED_PATH
Directory containing
.BR OED2.DAT .

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Volumes/OED2/OED2.DAT
Default primary CD-ROM mount location on macOS.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/oed/headwords.tsv
Cached TSV index of all normalized and display headwords.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/oed/oed_decompress.so
Compiled C decompression acceleration library.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Look up a word:
.B python3 oed.py lookup telescope
.TP
Look up a word with all historical quotations:
.B python3 oed.py lookup computer --all
.TP
View raw SGML for an entry:
.B python3 oed.py lookup byte --raw
.TP
Search words ending in "og":
.B python3 oed.py end og
.TP
Search single root words ending in "phobia":
.B python3 oed.py end phobia --single
.TP
Search words ending in "logy", sorted by length:
.B python3 oed.py end logy --len
.TP
Full-text search across all definitions and citations:
.B python3 oed.py text "slide rule"
.TP
Full-text search with match limit:
.B python3 oed.py text pin -n 50
.TP
Pipe raw SGML output into grep:
.B python3 oed.py lookup algorithm --raw --no-pager | grep '<qd>'
.TP
Start interactive shell:
.B python3 oed.py shell

